-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/99231016-3cfe-5cdb-a229-cab4411fbf82
-- title:
--   Supersingular DVR, Drinfeld affine chart and q+1 nodes, q=3
-- statement:
--   **Modular data.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (this auxiliary prime serves only as a guard on the level). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $= \kappa(j, j_{M'})$ over $\kappa$ (here a place is a valuation subring containing the constants, not all of the field, and a principal ideal ring), and let `hW` say that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those places $w$ that are rational (the constants surject onto the residue field of $w$), that are affine geometric places, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` lies in the supersingular $j$-set in characteristic $q$. Let `hle` assert the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'`, the first being the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q\bigl(\,j(d\tau) : d \mid M'\,\bigr)$, the second the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times\bigr)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of elements of non-zero residue, and with the normalisation that every non-zero element becomes of non-zero residue after scaling by a constant. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   **Small constants.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, and write $A_{k_0}$ for the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ obtained by comapping $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` require: $A_{k_0}$ is a discrete valuation ring; its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; it is henselian; its residue field is algebraically closed; and every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c \in k_0 \cap A$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; let $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and let $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lie in $A$ and satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base layer.** Let $K_b$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, so $K_b = k_0$; let $A_b$ be a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, and let $\varpi_b \in A_b$ be non-zero and generate the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   Throughout the conclusion $k_0$ acts on `fieldBar q M'` through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ characterised by the stated equivalence: $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$. Then there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) $W_0$ meets $k_0$ in $A$: for $x \in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) $W_0$ lies over $s$: for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has no pole at any place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ (the image of `jq`) has none, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between the image of $g$ and $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (5) $W_0$ is level-stable: for every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, and every $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in F_0$, one has $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in W_0$. (Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ selected by the $q$-expansion compatibility `IsLevelAutBar`, the identity if no such automorphism exists.)
--
--   (6) There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that, writing $L = k_0(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ for the compositum inside `fieldBar q M'` of the $k_0$-subextension generated by the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$:
--
--   (6a) the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a \in K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ in `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (6b) $B \subseteq L$;
--
--   (6c) $L$ is the fraction field of $B$: every $f \in L$ satisfies $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6e) every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$;
--
--   (6f) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime;
--
--   (6g) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\varpi_b$: $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\varpi_b \nmid h$;
--
--   (6h) the image of $j$ lies in $B$;
--
--   (6i) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6j) there is an element $b \in F_0 \cap B$ which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A$, having $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal whenever $\pi_0 \in V$, containing $j$, and such that $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$ (that is, such that the reduction of $j$ at $V$ is transcendental);
--
--   (6k) for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is an element $b \in F_0 \cap B$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that meets $k_0$ in $A$ and lies over $s'$ in the sense of (4) (with $V$ and $s'$ in place of $W_0$ and $s$);
--
--   (6l) for every $\overline{\mathbb F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure `Algebra (GaloisField q 2) κ`, every hypothesis that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the fraction field of the Drinfeld coordinate ring, of the subgroup generated by the `hFunctionFieldAction` of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ with $\zeta' \in C_s$) such that: $\#C_s = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\ q\ M'\ s$, where `placeWidthChar` is $\mathrm{jWidthChar}_q$ of the $j$-value of $s$ divided by the ramification index $\mathrm{ord}_s(j - j(s))$, and for $q = 3$ one has $\mathrm{jWidthChar}_3(j) = 6$ if $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise; $\ker \rho = (\varpi_b)$; on constants $\rho$ is reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ followed by the structure map $\kappa \to$ `quotField`; every element of `quotField` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $\rho(h) \ne 0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of the elements of `quotField` lying in the image of the Drinfeld coordinate ring in the Drinfeld function field; and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma, 1) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,u) \mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$) and $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` $f \in B$, the image $\rho(\,$`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹`$f)$ equals the action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma, 1)$ through `hFunctionFieldAction` on $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6m) there exists a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ such that:
--
--   — $\#\,$`nodes` $= q+1$;
--
--   — the level automorphisms permute the nodes: for every $\zeta$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O \in$ `nodes` there is $O' \in$ `nodes` with $f \in O \iff$ `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in O'$ for all $f \in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f \in F_0$;
--
--   — the action is transitive: for every $\zeta$ and all $O, O' \in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ realising the same equivalence between $O$ and $O'$;
--
--   — distinct nodes are distinguished: for $O \ne O'$ in `nodes` there is $f \in F_0$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--
--   — every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that meets $k_0$ in $A$ and lies over $s$ in the sense of (4) either contains $B$ (every $f \in B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$) or dominates a node: there is $O \in$ `nodes` with $O \subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   — and every $O \in$ `nodes` satisfies: $O \subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $O$ meets $k_0$ in $A$; every $f \in O$ is congruent to a constant, i.e. there is $x \in k_0 \cap A$ with $x \in O$ and $f - x$ a non-unit of $O$; and there exist an integer $E_0 \ge 1$, a witness that $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\, v$ for some $v \in k_0$ with $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$, the membership of $\pi_0$ in $O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_{k_0}$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, that is $\widehat{A_{k_0}}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   (i) $c_x c_y = \pi_0^{E_0} u$ in $O$;
--
--   (ii) $\iota$ carries each constant $x \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ to the corresponding constant of the crossing model;
--
--   (iii) $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\, U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\, V$;
--
--   (iv) $c_y \in W_0$ and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$;
--
--   (v) there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with: $O \subseteq W_x$; $W_x$ meets $k_0$ in $A$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; there is $t \in W_x$ whose reduction is transcendental, in the sense that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then all coefficients of $p$ do; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ does not; and for every $g \in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which has no pole at any place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ where $j$ has none, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when the $R_0$-residue of $g$ vanishes, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ then that image lies in $O$ and, for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ lying in $O$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between the image of $g$ and $c$ is a non-unit of $O$;
--
--   (vi) there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: every $f \in B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$; every $f \in B_x$ has no pole at any place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ where the image of $j$ has none; $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ in the sense that $f \in O$ if and only if $f h = g$ with $g, h \in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$ whenever $h \in O$; every $f \in F_0$ is a ratio of elements of $B_x$ with non-zero denominator; $B_x$ is generated as a subring by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set $T$; and there is $b \in B_x$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which meets $k_0$ in $A$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with $p(j)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, and does not contain $O$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ instance, at a rigid auxiliary level (a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \bmod 12$ dividing $M'$), of the local description of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ mod $q$, at a supersingular point $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$: a discrete valuation ring on the level field lying over $s$, an affine chart $B$ formally smooth of finite presentation over the base discrete valuation ring whose special fibre is identified with the function field of a Drinfeld quotient curve, and the $q+1$ nodes of that fibre, each with its crossing-model completion $\widehat{A}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$. It is deduced from the variant [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd), which carries the same hypotheses and further conclusions, and it is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeChart_point_specializes_iff_adicCompletion_stalk_of_normalModel_gen_j_local_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
